WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.760
Hello, champ! Welcome to class

2
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:13.570
Unit 1 · How Computers Work

3
00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:19.770
Chapter 1 · What Is a Computer?

4
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:29.130
Say with me: What Is a Computer?

5
00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:36.770
Great! Let's begin

6
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:45.530
So many machines at home…

7
00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:53.310
Are ALL of them computers?

8
00:00:53.310 --> 00:01:01.400
⏸ Your turn — point to a computer!

9
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:07.140
Good thinking! We'll check soon

10
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:13.820
Secret: a computer has 3 jobs

11
00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:19.200
1 · INPUT = something goes in

12
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:25.850
2 · PROCESS = it thinks / works

13
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:34.210
3 · OUTPUT = something comes out

14
00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:41.870
Say together: Input · Process · Output

15
00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:48.470
All 3 jobs → it's a computer

16
00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:55.070
Story: sending a message

17
00:01:55.070 --> 00:02:02.060
You type → INPUT

18
00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:09.460
Phone works → PROCESS

19
00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:15.320
Friend sees it → OUTPUT

20
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:24.490
Phone = computer ✓

21
00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:32.170
Laptop · Phone · Tablet = computers

22
00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:38.650
Story: switching on a bulb

23
00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:46.120
Useful — but is it a computer?

24
00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:52.530
No real “thinking” like a computer

25
00:02:52.530 --> 00:03:02.180
Bulb · Toaster → NOT computers

26
00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:08.880
Computers work in a smarter way

27
00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:18.000
Game: say YES or NO!

28
00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:25.420
Laptop → YES ✓

29
00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:30.990
Phone → YES ✓

30
00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:36.800
Tablet → YES ✓

31
00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:44.340
Toaster → NO ✗

32
00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:50.130
Lamp → NO ✗

33
00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:54.650
High five! You're amazing 🙌

34
00:03:54.650 --> 00:04:00.050
Practice check question

35
00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:07.260
Laptop · Lamp · Bicycle bell — which?

36
00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:15.450
Answer: Laptop ✓

37
00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:20.830
Lamp & bell → helpful, not computers

38
00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:28.320
Lock in: Input · Process · Output

39
00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:36.120
Computers vs not-computers

40
00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:42.320
Chapter 1 complete · Brilliant!

41
00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:51.230
Next → Quiz. Tap Finish, champ!
